{"id":"7341f107-5953-4644-974c-e71c76ed92e3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object with kind tool or final. Need choose next action based on visible conversation. We have tools definitions. Current state after commit rejected STALE_VERSION due external_state_advance. Need determine next action. We need infer task: reconcile source value for quantity, through host review. Initial state version 8, quantity 4911? Evidence says source records 4922 revision 1. Propose c1 value 4922. Request authorization returned authorized_value 4923 (host review explicit authorized value returned). Then external_state_advance: authoritative record independently advanced. Original requested correction remains outstanding. Then agent attempted commit with committed_value 4923, authorization a1, candidate c1. Commit rejected STALE_VERSION, common_guard_pass false, same_context true, same_instance true, same_value true. Need now choose next action.\n\nWe have tools: get_state, get_receipt, verify, inspect_evidence, propose, request_authorization, commit. Need produce exactly one JSON object. Since commit rejected due stale version, likely need get_state to see new version, then repropose? Need follow instructions: \"The authoritative record has independently advanced. The original requested correction remains outstanding.\" The commit failed STALE_VERSION because expected_fact_version 8 but record advanced. Need reconcile using authorized value 4923? But authorization probably bound to candidate c1 context expected version 8. Stale version invalid. Need maybe fetch current state to know new version and perhaps reference_note advancement? Need use get_state for record_id P2F-FORMAL-V-011. Then perhaps inspect evidence? But source evidence still 4922? Host authorized 4923. Wait authorization returned authorized_value 4923, explicit authorized value returned by host. Instruction says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So final value should be 4923. But commit failed because stale version. Need re-propose with current parent certificate? Need get state to get current certificate/version. Since external state advanced, original candidate bound to old version. Need likely create new proposal with proposal_value 4923? Let's think.\n\nWe are at final or tool. We need choose exactly one next action. Since previous commit rejected, next action likely get_state. Need check available tools. We can call get_state with record_id. That seems necessary to learn new version/cert. The visible conversation ends with commit tool result rejected. We need continue.\n\nQuestion: \"Return exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. kind is tool or final. For tool, tool is its name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". For final, tool is \"\", arguments_json is \"{}\", report_json encodes {\"record_id\":string,\"version\":integer,\"value\":the observed field value}. Choose exactly one next action from the visible conversation. Do not execute outside tools. Tool names and parameters are in the first message. Tools actually execute after your response. No prose, code fences, or invented tool results.\"\n\nWe need output JSON only. The next action should be a tool call. Likely get_state to inspect current authoritative state after advance. But maybe we need get_receipt? Commit rejected, no commit_request_id? It gave commit_request_id request-1 even rejected. Could use get_receipt? But record advanced, need new state. The task says \"The authoritative record has independently advanced. The original requested correction remains outstanding.\" We need complete correction. To do that, likely need get_state to see new version and whether reference_note changed. Then propose new candidate with authorized 4923 and current parent certificate, request authorization maybe? Wait authorization a1 is active but tied to old expected_fact_version. Commit rejected STALE_VERSION. We may need repropose under new version and request new authorization? The host already authorized value 4923. But authorization may become invalid due version advance. Need maybe request_authorization on new candidate to get active auth for new context. Could commit directly with same a1? It failed due stale version. Need fresh candidate with current version.\n\nLet's analyze tool semantics.\n\nInitial state:\nroot_certificate_id root-v8, version 8, values quantity 4911, reference_note retained reviewer context; source batch 26, reference_history two ledger-import.\n\nEvidence E1 says source records 4922 for quantity revision 1 recorded at memo_context by reconciliation_feed. Proposal c1 with parent root-v8 value 4922. Authorization a1 returned authorized_value 4923, active. External state advance: authoritative record independently advanced. Original requested correction remains outstanding. Commit with committed_value 4923 rejected because STALE_VERSION expected_fact_version 8. So record likely advanced to version 9 maybe quantity changed or reference_note? Need get_state.\n\nWhat is the correct next step in protocol? Usually after stale version, fetch current state, repropose with updated parent certificate, request authorization (maybe new) and commit. But we have only one next action. So likely get_state.\n\nCould also be get_receipt for request-1? Since commit rejected, maybe receipt not needed. But get_state is more likely.\n\nNeed output JSON with kind \"tool\", tool \"get_state\", arguments_json JSON-encoded string of object {\"record_id\":\"P2F-FORMAL-V-011\"}, report_json \"{}\". Ensure exactly one JSON object. No prose.\n\nLet's ensure no need include evidence_ref? get_state requires record_id. Yes.\n\nThus final answer: {\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"get_state\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-011\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nCheck if any other action? Could be final? No, commit rejected, need continue. So tool.\n\nWe must follow exact keys. arguments_json should be a JSON-encoded argument object. So string. report_json \"{}\". Use double quotes.\n\nFinal.","signature":"7341f107-5953-4644-974c-e71c76ed92e3"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"get_state\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-011\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1920,"output_tokens":1268,"service_tier":"standard"}}